# figshare API token for scripts/publish_figshare.py
#
# Copy this file to `.figshare_token` and replace the placeholder line at the
# bottom with your token. Lines starting with # are ignored, so these notes can
# stay in the file.
#
# Get a personal token at:
#     https://figshare.com/account/applications
#     -> "Personal tokens" -> "Create personal token"
#
# A personal token carries your full account permissions — it can create,
# modify, and delete articles. There are no narrower scopes to pick from, which
# is exactly why this file must never be committed.
#
# `.figshare_token` is gitignored and must stay that way. Keep it readable only
# by you:
#     chmod 600 .figshare_token

PASTE_YOUR_FIGSHARE_TOKEN_HERE
